          %h2#universal_property Universal property
          %p
            We spell out that def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory"}
            indeed satisfies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            that defines the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
          #WhiteheadTheoremInModelCategories.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+theorem"} Whitehead theorem
                in model categories)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibrant+objects"} bifibrant objects
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine99"} Goerss-Jardine 99, part I, theorem 1.10
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By the factorization axioms in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \longrightarrow Y
              factors through an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
              as an acyclic cofibration followed by an acyclic fibration. In particular it follows that with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              both
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibrant+object"} bifibrant
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            %p
              So let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
              be an acyclic fibration between fibrant-cofibrant objects, the case of acyclic cofibrations is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+inverse"} right inverse
              given by a lift
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}
              in the diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ∅
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi cof
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mn 1
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi Fib
                                  %mo ∩
                                  %mi W
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\emptyset &amp;\rightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\in cof}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;{}^{{f^{-1}}}\nearrow&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in Fib \cap W}}
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;=&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              To see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}
              is also a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+inverse"} left inverse
              up to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cyl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cyl(X)
              be any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder object
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiagonal"} codiagonal
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              as a cofibration followed by a an acyclic fibration
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ι
                          %mi X
                    %mi Cyl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi σ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \sqcup X \stackrel{\iota_X}{\longrightarrow} Cyl(X) \stackrel{\sigma}{\longrightarrow} X
            %p and consider the square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ⊔
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mn 1
                                %mo ∘
                                %mi f
                                %mo ,
                                %mi id
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ι
                                    %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi Cof
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi W
                                  %mo ∩
                                  %mi Fib
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Cyl
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi f
                                %mo ∘
                                %mi σ
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X \sqcup X
                    \&amp;\stackrel{(f^{-1}\circ f, id)}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\iota_X}}{}_{\mathllap{\in Cof}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}_{\mathrlap{\in W \cap Fib}}
                    \\\
                    Cyl(X) &amp;\underset{f\circ \sigma}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              which
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commutes
              due to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}
              being a genuine right inverse of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              now admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} lift
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi f
                      %msub
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mi L
                      %mi id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta \colon f^{-1}\circ f \Rightarrow_L id
          #FibrantCofibrantReplacementFunctorToHomotopyCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %em choice
              for each object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{C}
              of
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a factorization
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ∅
                        %munderover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi Cof
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mi X
                        %mi Q
                        %mi X
                        %munderover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi W
                            %mo ∩
                            %mi Fib
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mi x
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \underoverset{\in Cof}{i_X}{\longrightarrow} Q X \underoverset{\in W \cap Fib}{p_x}{\longrightarrow} X
                  of the initial morphism, such that when
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is already cofibrant then
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mi X
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi id
                            %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_X = id_X
              %li
                %p
                  a factorization
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %munderover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi W
                            %mo ∩
                            %mi Cof
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi j
                              %mi X
                        %mi R
                        %mi X
                        %munderover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi Fib
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi q
                              %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \underoverset{\in W \cap Cof}{j_X}{\longrightarrow} R X \underoverset{\in Fib}{q_x}{\longrightarrow} \ast
                  of the terminal morphism, such that when
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is already fibrant then
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi j
                            %mi X
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi id
                            %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_X = id_X
            %p Write then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
