            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              The construction in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FibrantCofibrantReplacementFunctorToHomotopyCategory"}
              is indeed well defined.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              First of all, the object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mi Q
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Q X
              is indeed both fibrant and cofibrant (as well as related by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zag"} zig-zag
              of weak equivalences to
              = succeed "):" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ∅
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi Cof
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi Cof
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi W
                                %mo ∩
                                %mi Cof
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mi Q
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi Fib
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi W
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\emptyset
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\in Cof}}\downarrow &amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{\in Cof}}
                    \\\
                    Q X &amp;\underset{\in W \cap Cof}{\longrightarrow}&amp; R Q X &amp;\underset{\in Fib}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \ast
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\in W}}\downarrow
                    \\\
                    X
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now to see that the image on morphisms is well defined. First observe that any two choices
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Q
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Q f)_{i}
              of the first lift in the definition are left homotopic to each other, exhibited by lifting in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                            %mi X
                            %mo ⊔
                            %mi Q
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi Q
                                %mi f
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi Q
                                %mi f
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
