          #EssentialUniquenessOfLocalizationFunctorOfModelCategory.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Due to theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalPropertyOfHomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory"}
              we may suppress the choices of cofibrant
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              and fibrant replacement
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FibrantCofibrantReplacementFunctorToHomotopyCategory"}
              and just speak of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+functor"} localization functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\gamma \;\colon\;
                    \\mathcal{C}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Ho(\mathcal{C})
            %p
              up to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
          %p
            While the construction of the homotopy category in def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory"}
            combines the restriction to good (fibrant/cofibrant) objects with the passage to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
            of morphisms, it is often useful to consider intermediate stages:
          #FullSubcategoriesOfFibrantCofibrantObjects.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mi fc
                        %mtr
