                    \\,.
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              preserves acyclic cofibrations, then the diagram on the right has a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} lift
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi L
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L\dashv R)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of that lift is a lift of the left diagram. This shows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(g)
              has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              against all acylic cofibrations and hence is a fibration. Conversely, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              preserves fibrations, the same argument run from right to left gives that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              preserves acyclic fibrations.
            %p Now by repeatedly applying (i) and (ii), all four conditions in question are seen to be equivalent.
          #QuillenEquivalence.num_defn
            %h6#definition_10 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}, \mathcal{D}
              two
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              (def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenAdjunction"}>
              )
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi L
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (L \dashv R)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\mathcal{C}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{L}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\longrightarrow}}
                    \\mathcal{D}
            %p
              is called a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              if the following equivalent conditions hold.
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+derived+functor"} right derived functor
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  (via prop.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConditionsOnQuillenAdjunctionAreIndeedEquivalent"}
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftAndRightDerivedFunctors"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒟
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathbb{R}R \colon Ho(\mathcal{C}) \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} Ho(\mathcal{D})
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+derived+functor"} left derived functor
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                  (via prop.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConditionsOnQuillenAdjunctionAreIndeedEquivalent"}
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftAndRightDerivedFunctors"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝕃
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒟
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathbb{L}L \colon Ho(\mathcal{D}) \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} Ho(\mathcal{C})
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  For every cofibrant object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒟
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \mathcal{D}
                  and every fibrant object
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathcal{C}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \longrightarrow R(c)
                  is a weak equivalence precisely if its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
                  morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(c) \to d
                  is
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi d
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %msub
                                  %mi W
                                  %mi 𝒟
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %msub
                                  %mi W
                                  %mi 𝒞
                            %mi c
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\frac{
                        d \overset{\in W_{\mathcal{D}}}{\longrightarrow} R(c)
                        }{
                        L(d) \overset{\in W_{\mathcal{C}}}{\longrightarrow} c
                        }
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  For every cofibrant object
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\in \mathcal{C}
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+adjunction+unit"} derived adjunction unit
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi fib
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        d \longrightarrow R(L(d)) \longrightarrow R(L(d)^{fib})
                %p
                  (of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
                  with any
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+replacement"} fibrant replacement
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
              %li
                %p
                  For every fibrant object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathcal{C}
                  the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+adjunction+counit"} derived adjunction counit
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi cof
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        L(R(c)^{cof}) \longrightarrow L(R(c)) \longrightarrow c
                %p
                  (of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+counit"} adjunction counit
                  with any
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+replacement"} cofibrant replacement
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
          #QuillenAdjunctionInducesAdjunctionOnHomotopyCategories.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+adjunction"}> derived adjunction
                )
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi Qu
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊥
                          %mi Qu
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi L
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \underoverset{\underset{R}{\longrightarrow}}{\overset{L}{\longleftarrow}}{{}_{\phantom{Qu}}\bot_{Qu}}\mathcal{D}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              between
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
              form a pair of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝕃
                          %mi L
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ho(\mathcal{C})
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{\mathbb{R}R}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{\mathbb{L}L}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    Ho(\mathcal{D})
            %p
              between the corresponding
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy categories
            %p
              Moreover, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+counit"} adjunction counit
              of this derived adjunction are the images of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+adjunction+unit"} derived adjunction unit
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+adjunction+counit"} derived adjunction counit
              of the original
